  "overview": {
    "description": "Traversone (also Rovescino, CiapanÃ², Tressette a Perdere) is an Italian reverse trick-taking game where players try to AVOID taking point cards. It uses the Tressette ranking (3-2-A high) and scoring system, but the goal is inverted â€” whoever accumulates the MOST points loses. A 'Cappotto' (sweep) reverses the penalty to opponents.",
